WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.167
Tonight, the top U.S.

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.303
general, Mark Milley, is giving his take

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.471
on another chapter

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:04.971
in the Trump

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:07.073
classified documents investigation.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.241
This was reporting

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.776
that CNN broke last week

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:10.243
that the former

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:11.444
president recorded

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:13.880
was recorded in July 2021

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.814
indicating that

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.916
he had a classified Pentagon document

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.552
pertaining to a potential attack on Iran.

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:20.520
And implying

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.321
that it would counter

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:22.455
what his top general,

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.424
Mark Milley, was saying.

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.959
Those comments were apparently

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.360
in response to a New Yorker

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.194
article

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.262
saying that Milley had warned

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.264
Trump against striking Iran.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.033
Reportedly telling Trump, quote,

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.402
You're going to have a f ing war.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.669
Senator Lieberman spoke

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.872
exclusively with General Mark Milley,

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:39.873
who was only willing to say

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:43.676
this about that investigation.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.145
The former president suggested

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:46.379
in a book by Mark Meadows

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.348
that it was your desire to attack Iran.

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:49.649
And he was saying no.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:50.617
Is that what happened?

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:52.118
Well, I'll be

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.120
entirely inappropriate or thankfully,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.255
I prepared to comment on that.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:55.488
It'd be

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.090
entirely inappropriate for me

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.325
to comment on the ongoing

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.427
federal investigation,

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:02.762
and I'm not going to do that now.

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.230
So not even to clarify

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.732
what happened there.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.367
No, I think it's inappropriate.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.235
There's an ongoing federal investigation,

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.103
and I'm not going to comment

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:10.703
one way or another

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:14.074
on any of the issues concerning that.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.008
Let's get more insight

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.142
tonight from former Trump

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.611
national security adviser John Bolton.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:19.746
And thank you, Ambassador,

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:20.447
for being here.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:22.015
You heard from General Milley.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:22.649
They're weighing in.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.316
We do know

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:24.150
from our reporting

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.251
that he has spoken

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.187
to investigators in this case.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:29.289
But when it comes to this document

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.058
that Trump allegedly had on plans

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.960
to potentially strike Iran.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.494
Do you know

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:35.862
which which document

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.564
Trump could have been holding in his

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:38.731
hands during this recording?

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:41.701
Well, I don't

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:42.168
I don't think

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:45.271
there's any way of knowing and

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:48.341
given Trump's propensity to overstate

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:49.776
things.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.077
It's entirely possible

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:52.378
he was holding in his hand

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.246
something like

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.180
the lunch menu

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.850
from the Bedminster Grill that day

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.219
and that he was embellishing on what

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.121
what a document

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.589
that Mark Milley might have prepared

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:03.223
would say.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:04.290
So this goes

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.992
to a pretty fundamental point.

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:07.293
I don't have any doubt

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.561
there are very sensitive

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:09.796
documents involved here.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:12.198
But until you actually see them,

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.400
I think it's important

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.503
not to kind of overhype

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.304
what what may be at stake here,

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.405
particularly with Trump,

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:20.907
who is propensity to bluster.

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:22.408
There's actually a better word for that

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:23.543
I won't use on TV,

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.712
but his propensity to bluster

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.147
is unending.

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:27.380
Well,

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.249
I think there's concern from prosecutors

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:29.582
here, though,

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.850
because they clearly

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.085
want to know more about this.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.586
I mean, they brought the chairman

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:34.854
of the Joint Chiefs of Staff

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.222
in to talk about it.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.423
And, of course,

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:38.324
we don't actually know

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.359
which document Trump

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:41.060
was holding at that time,

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.829
if he was simply referencing

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:43.563
this document.

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:44.998
But what our reporting did show

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.166
is that the Justice

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:47.700
Department wanted this document

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:48.902
and they sent a subpoena

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.470
they made clear to Trump's attorneys,

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.304
I was told

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.772
that they wanted this document

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.707
specifically that he was talking about

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:55.275
on tape.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.543
But Trump's attorneys

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:57.877
could not locate the document

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:58.545
to produce it.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:00.780
So if he was holding that document

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.215
and they were unable to find it

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.283
and there is a document

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:05.285
related to Iran out there,

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:06.452
how much does that concern you

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.321
about how it could compromise the U.S.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:09.255
national security

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.526
Well, if it were an actual

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:16.496
document that the Pentagon produced as

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.599
as a war plan, that would be one thing.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.869
If it's simply Trump making it up

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:24.437
as he goes along.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.471
That could explain

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.673
why they can't find it,

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.074
because it never existed.

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.576
I mean, the other explanation

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:30.877
is he destroyed it.

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:33.213
And that would be a very serious matter

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:34.113
because it would show,

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.081
I think, clearly

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:35.582
a guilty

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.883
intent that he had a

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.918
highly classified document

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:42.388
at The idea that that

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.224
that you can take, though,

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:46.192
the real official documents

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:47.827
the Pentagon works on

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.395
and kind of spread them around

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:50.496
even to the president,

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.232
I would be very surprised at that.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:54.567
They are understandably kept

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.502
very tightly held,

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.972
infrequently taken away from the Pentagon

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.173
and usually removed

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.474
from the Situation Room

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:02.642
or the Oval Office

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:03.743
with great care

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:04.877
when the people

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.846
who brought them over leave.

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:07.747
And I should note that

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:10.250
you also have a level of concern here.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.184
The Justice Department

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:14.821
charged a suspected Iranian operative

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.923
last year for allegedly

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.458
plotting to assassinate you.

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:19.425
But on this front of

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.261
when it comes to the relationship

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:22.962
that Trump had with General Milley,

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:24.697
what were your observations

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.432
about Trump's views

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.634
toward Chairman Milley?

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:30.870
Well, when

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:31.938
I was at the White House,

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:33.873
this was in the period where

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:36.476
where the successor to General

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:37.176
Joe Dunford,

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:39.212
who was the chairman of the Joint Chiefs

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:39.746
at the beginning

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:41.381
of the administration, was going on.

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:43.182
And my own personal view

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.317
was that Mark Milley

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:46.486
should be chairman of the Joint Chiefs.

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:47.053
It happened

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:49.289
that the Trump agreed with that

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:50.523
and appointed him.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:51.324
And I think

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.091
at the beginning

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.760
he was enthusiastic

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:54.827
that it was a good choice.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.297
And I certainly believe that at the time

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:59.165
I was gone,

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:00.266
I think when a lot of this

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:02.302
interesting material happened.

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:04.570
But it's obvious that relationship

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:05.972
between Milley and Trump

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.408
soured as Trump's relationship

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:10.543
with so many other people soured.

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:13.079
As we see these investigations ramp up or

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:13.946
we're going to wait

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:14.213
to see

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:15.048
what the special counsel

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:16.816
does on this document investigation.

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:18.184
Trump is still the frontrunner

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:19.585
for the Republican nomination

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:20.353
for president.

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:21.020
You've said you're

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.822
considering a 2024 run.

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:24.457
Have you made a decision on that yet?

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:27.193
No, I haven't.

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:27.560
I want to

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.629
I want to see what what happens

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:31.064
with some of the other announcements.

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:34.367
I would not do this frivolously or merely

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:35.501
to criticize

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:36.969
Trump's performance in office,

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.671
although that would be,

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.673
I think, an extensive job to do.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:41.240
It would be

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.443
with the serious intent to win.

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:44.377
I think it's critical

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:45.578
for the Republican Party

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:47.480
absolute critical

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.748
and for the country as well

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:50.450
that Trump did not get our nomination.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.418
I think in a race against Biden,

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:54.420
as unpopular as Biden is.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.621
Trump might well win.

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.724
So I think this is a serious matter

00:05:57.724 --> 00:05:59.158
that the Republicans

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:00.226
are going to have to deal with.

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:01.194
I wouldn't

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.795
count on a day of sex

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:02.962
and a

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:03.863
like an indictment

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:06.032
in the classified documents case.

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:07.967
To save us on this.

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.035
Knowing Trump,

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:11.437
he may well turn it into an asset.

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:13.005
How soon do you think you need

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.540
to make a decision on like that?

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.375
Like on this,

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:16.476
since we're seeing how big

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:17.343
the field is getting

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:20.380
Well, frankly, that's

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.514
another consideration

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:21.881
if there's

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.216
a small army of people

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:25.518
wandering around seeking the nomination.

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:27.987
I don't think there would be a case

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:29.355
that I would be adding anything.

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:30.957
But but I think it's still early.

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:33.126
I think this is a very strange cycle.

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:34.026
And I think honestly,

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.294
in the next 90 days,

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:35.728
it's a

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:36.863
it's a two man race

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:39.165
between Governor DeSantis and Trump.

00:06:39.165 --> 00:06:40.600
I think

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.300
knowing Trump

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:41.834
as I do,

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:43.202
that he will unload

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:45.271
on DeSantis unceasingly.

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:47.073
He's already started.

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:48.441
And I think Governor DeSantis

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:50.443
has got to come back with his case

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:50.810
as to

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:51.444
why Trump's

00:06:51.444 --> 00:06:52.812
not qualified to be president.

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:54.147
And that's really

00:06:54.147 --> 00:06:55.681
a marker for everybody else

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:56.449
who might get in.

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:57.183
You're not going to get

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:58.751
the Republican nomination

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:00.753
by picking away at the other opponents.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:02.321
You're going to win the nomination

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:03.990
by taking Trump on directly

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:04.957
and beating him.

00:07:04.957 --> 00:07:06.292
Well, they're not really taking

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:07.126
Trump out directly.

00:07:07.126 --> 00:07:07.293
I mean,

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:08.961
we saw eight of the candidates

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.563
Trump in the night in Iowa

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:11.330
over the weekend,

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:13.533
and none of them would really directly

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:15.101
say his name when they were on stage.

00:07:15.101 --> 00:07:16.002
Do you think it's a mistake

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:17.804
for candidates like Governor DeSantis

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:19.605
to not directly

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:21.140
criticize Trump in this race?

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:24.210
100%.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:24.877
This is not

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:25.344
an issue

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:26.679
about philosophy

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:28.781
because Trump has no philosophy

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.183
and it's not really an issue

00:07:30.183 --> 00:07:32.852
about his personality or his temperament.

00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:34.320
It's about his competence

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.422
to be president, which he does not have.

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:37.156
And I think

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:38.491
unless you make that point

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:42.528
effectively to voters and ignore the £800

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:43.663
gorilla,

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:45.598
it's impossible to make that case.

00:07:45.598 --> 00:07:46.566
So I think the person

00:07:46.566 --> 00:07:47.767
who ultimately wins

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:49.268
the Republican nomination

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:50.937
is the person who beats Trump.

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:52.939
And as you say and I agree,

00:07:52.939 --> 00:07:54.540
I don't think anybody has stepped up

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:55.174
to that role.

00:07:55.174 --> 00:07:56.209
Maybe Chris Christie.

00:07:56.209 --> 00:07:58.010
Well, God bless him. If he does.

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.812
But if he doesn't, somebody needs to.

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:01.347
My in my case, though,

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:03.182
it would be not just to do that,

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:05.084
but to win the nomination.

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:06.886
We'll see what you decide ultimately.

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:08.254
I know you were listening

00:08:08.254 --> 00:08:09.121
to the top of the show

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.022
as we were talking about this

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:12.692
new CNN reporting on investigators

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:13.693
looking into a pool

00:08:13.693 --> 00:08:15.328
that was drained at Mar a Lago

00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:16.829
and then flooded a room

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:18.231
that has the computer servers

00:08:18.231 --> 00:08:19.866
that store the surveillance footage

00:08:19.866 --> 00:08:22.034
that we know prosecutors have subpoenaed.

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:22.468
Of course,

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:23.936
still a lot of questions about that.

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:25.638
But what was your reaction

00:08:25.638 --> 00:08:26.439
to hearing that

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:30.676
Well, I think the prosecutors are right

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:31.744
to be suspicious

00:08:31.744 --> 00:08:32.712
of of Trump

00:08:32.712 --> 00:08:35.248
and his capacity to obstruct justice.

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:37.884
This particular episode Frank, frankly,

00:08:38.251 --> 00:08:39.819
struck me as a little Rube

00:08:39.819 --> 00:08:41.120
Goldberg like

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.488
but but not beyond

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:43.389
the realm of the possible.

00:08:43.389 --> 00:08:44.957
I don't remember the geography

00:08:44.957 --> 00:08:45.825
of the architecture

00:08:45.825 --> 00:08:47.460
enough to understand

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:48.594
how draining the pool

00:08:48.594 --> 00:08:49.729
would have flooded this room.

00:08:49.729 --> 00:08:51.230
But but it's look,

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:53.466
you've got to pursue every lead in a case

00:08:53.466 --> 00:08:54.166
that's serious.

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:55.301
There's no doubt about it.

00:08:55.301 --> 00:08:57.570
It may turn out not to represent anything

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:59.672
or it may we don't know.

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:00.806
There's a lot we don't know.

00:09:00.806 --> 00:09:02.074
And that may be part of it.

00:09:02.074 --> 00:09:03.442
Yeah. A lot of questions remain.

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:04.377
Ambassador John Bolton,

00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:05.444
thank you for your time tonight.

